Medical history:
{"medical_history": {"chief_complaint": "The patient presents with a history of seizures since the age of 2.", "family_history": "There is no history of epilepsy or seizures in the family. The patient's parents were non-consanguineous.", "history_of_present_illness": "The first epileptic event involved sudden loss of awareness, generalized clonic movements, and sialorrhea, with no fever or other symptoms. From age 20 to the present, the patient experienced focal onset impaired awareness seizures characterized by coughing aura, staring, mouth automatisms, bimanual automatisms, and head shift to the left. These seizures lasted about 1 minute, with secondary generalizations occurring rarely (four times in lifetime). The awake seizures occurred two to three times per week and worsened premenstrually. A second type of event included sleep episodes of agitation and frenetic rubbing of the left ear, averaging one to two times per week.", "past_medical_history": "The patient has had several antiseizure drug trials with medications including valproate, phenytoin, lamotrigine, and phenobarbital, with seizure control being variable. Current medications include carbamazepine and clobazam, which have not achieved seizure freedom.", "social_history": "Not specified."}}

