{"physical_examinations": [{"changes_over_time": "Not specified", "date": "Not specified", "relevant_findings": "Neurological function assessments revealed a Mini-Mental State Examination (MMSE) score of 29, a Montreal Cognitive Assessment (MoCA) score of 25 (indicative of mild cognitive dysfunction), a Hamilton Depression Scale (HAMD) score of 12 (suggestive of possible anxiety), and a Hamilton Anxiety Scale (HAMA) score of 3 (within normal range). No notable facial features or positive signs were observed during cardiac, pulmonary, abdominal, or neurological examinations.", "vital_signs": "Not specified"}]}

