Physical examination:
{"physical_examinations": [{"changes_over_time": "At postoperative day 21, the ROM was 10\u00b0-110\u00b0 and HKAa was corrected to valgus 16\u00b0 on the right and left knees. At 1-year follow-up, the knee ROM was 5\u00b0-125\u00b0 with HKAa of valgus 13\u00b0 and 17\u00b0. Annual follow-ups showed almost fixed-knee ROM (10\u00b0-125\u00b0) with HKAa of valgus 11\u00b0 and 16\u00b0. At the latest follow-up (5 years), the ROM improved to 10\u00b0-135\u00b0 with an extension lag of 10\u00b0, and no evidence of loosening or fracture was observed.", "date": "Not specified", "relevant_findings": "Manual muscle testing showed grade 3/4 on the right and left knees. The range of motion (ROM) was 20\u00b0-150\u00b0, and the patella was laterally dislocated during knee flexion. Severe genu valgum of the right knee with a hip-knee-ankle angle (HKAa) of valgus 29.0\u00b0, grade IV osteoarthritic changes in the lateral femorotibial compartment, and laterally dislocated patella. Dysplasia of the lateral femoral condyle, dysplasia of the trochlea with a sulcus angle of 150\u00b0, laterally located patella, and a tibial tuberosity to trochlear groove distance of 41.3 mm.", "vital_signs": "Not specified"}]}

